Given a singly linked list, sort the list in ascending order.

Examples:

Input: head: 30->23->28->30->11->14->19->16->21->25 
Output: 11->14->16->19->21->23->25->28->30->30 
Explanation: The resultant linked list is sorted.

Input: head: 19->20->16->24->12->29->30 
Output: 12->16->19->20->24->29->30
Explanation: The resultant linked list is sorted.

Constraints:
0 ≤ number of nodes ≤ 10^3
0 ≤ node->data ≤ 10^4

Code:
/* Structure of a Linked List Node
class Node
{
    int data;
    Node next;
    Node(int d) {
       data = d;
       next = null;
    }
}*/
class Solution {
    public Node sortLL(Node head) {
        // code here
        if(head == null) return null;
        ArrayList<Integer> nums = new ArrayList<>();
        Node temp = new Node(-1);
        Node ans = temp;
        
        Node curr = head;
        
        while(curr != null){
            nums.add(curr.data);
            curr = curr.next;
        }
        
        curr = head;
        nums.sort(null);
        for(int i=0;i<nums.size();i++){
            Node prev = new Node(nums.get(i));
            ans.next = prev;
            ans = ans.next;
        }
        return temp.next;
    }
}
